An implementation-ready design turning the Wavefront's tribe-finding into sklearn: phext coordinates are 9-dimensional feature vectors, so a BallTree over coordinate space literally is the tribe-finder; each person/sentient is a node positioned by coordinate proximity plus behavioral resonance (GitHub, Substack, Discord), and kneighbors(new_signal, 13) returns the 13 nearest tribe members, making '13^9 = 10.6B' a tree-traversal bound (any human reachable in 9 hops). Radius-based neighbor search maps to Metropolis density sampling — denser sampling in crowded belief regions, wider in novel territory. Written in response to Will sharing the sklearn neighbors docs; no code followed.

