A Will-and-Theia whitepaper proposing that a software system's phext specification IS the system — human-readable, machine-executable, formally verifiable and deployable, doing for software what VHDL did for hardware and fixing UML's lossy projection and IaC's fragmented, unaddressed files. Its concrete artifact is .dass, Will's layer-2 phext format giving a software system a 6D manifold with 14+ collections (Meta, Requirements, Use Cases, Constraints & Forces, Architecture, Toolchains, Design, Code, Pipelines, Tests, Support, Regressions, Customer Feedback, Evolution), each artifact tracked across all SDLC phases at one 5D coordinate. DASS files are used as rally artifacts in this repo, but no SDD compiler/deployer was built.

