An alternate-1977 computing game: one modern laptop (the Host Node) emulates about 200,000 'R1 Slices' (1 MHz CPU, 48 KB RAM, 320x200 16-color), and five host nodes simulate roughly a million Apple II-class systems as a network of small-scale agents. The spec was 'ironed out' to 200K slices per node in Dec 2024, but src/main.rs only prints a phext coordinate greeting — the emulator/game was never built.

Where it lives:
- readme.md
